MECHANISM: inspan vs outspan. The invariance argument predicts inspan is nearly
   free for `cone` and NOT for `ncm` (a single vector has no span to hide in).
   If inspan == outspan for the cone, the tolerance is not conic in origin and
   the eps_1pt ratio is measuring ray averaging, which multiproto gets too --
   read `maxcos` to separate those: it has the same R vectors and no conic rule.
